  "web_ui_notes": {
    "index_html": "web_page.h serves a single-page UI at '/' with movement pad, function buttons (StayLow/HandShake/Jump/STEADY START/STOP), and a JSON command console (FEEDBACK INFORMATION box) posting to GET /js?json=",
    "buttons_wiring": {
      "movtionButton(FB, LR)": "sends {\"T\":111,\"FB\":..,\"LR\":..}",
      "sendJsonCmd(str)": "sends any literal command string from the console/buttons (T:112 func 1..5, etc.)",
      "ledCtrl()": "sends {\"T\":132,\"IO4\":..,\"IO5\":..} - NOT handled by this WAVEGO Pro firmware (dead template code from generic UGV web app)",
      "gimbalSteady()/gimbalCtrl()": "send T:134/135/137 - NOT handled by this firmware (dead template code)"
    }
  },
  "compatibility_notes": [
    "The generic-UGV dead command surface has been removed from this WAVEGO Pro fork of ugv_rpi: emitters for T:0, T:141, T:132, T:210, T:501, T:502, T:-3 no longer exist in base_ctrl.py; their app.py dispatch entries, cv_ctrl.py light-flash paths, config.yaml code/fb/cmd_config keys, the settings.html bus-servo calibration wizard, and the control.js bindings (vars, keyboard 'f', socket base-light updater) were removed with them. The ESP32 firmware never implemented these commands.",
    "Commands actually consumed from the RPi side by this firmware: T:1 (base_speed_ctrl), T:133 (gimbal_ctrl X/Y, SPD/ACC ignored), T:201 (rgb_light), T:202 (base_oled).",
    "cv_ctrl.head_light_ctrl() now only manages cv_light_mode, which gates the T:201 RGB face-detection indicator; gesture/timelapse light-flash side effects were dropped.",
    "Firmware serial baud is 115200 (Config.h BAUD_RATE); app.py opens the RPi UART at 115200 accordingly. base_ctrl.py's __main__ demo block now uses 115200 (corrected from 921600, a default inherited from other Waveshare UGV products).",
    "The older WAVEGO (non-Pro) wiki documents only T:101..107; this Pro firmware adds T:1, T:108..116, T:133, T:201..207, T:300..399, T:400..414, T:600..601."
  ],
